# Aseprite files
*.aseprite
*.ase
*.png
*.gif
*.jpg

# README showcase images (everything else in examples/ stays untracked)
!examples/swordsman/swordsman.png
!examples/swordsman/swordsman_slash.gif
!examples/swordsman/swordsman_slash_sheet.png

# Icon/tile SOURCES drawn via the aseprite MCP. These .aseprite files ARE the
# artwork — the ASCII grids they replaced were only ever a script's input, and
# the previous session's work was lost precisely because it stayed untracked.
!examples/icon-animation/*.aseprite
!examples/tileset/*.aseprite

# Exports are tracked too, as the permanent showcase. They are regenerable from
# the sources above, but "regenerable" needs Aseprite installed and running —
# tracking them is what makes the art viewable on GitHub and in a plain clone.
# `<name>.png` is the real 1x asset; `<name>_x8.png` is the 8x nearest-neighbour
# render for viewing, since 16px art is invisible on a modern display.
!examples/icon-animation/*.png
!examples/tileset/*.png
!examples/tileset/*.gif

# Third-party reference sheets, vendored deliberately for measuring pixel-art
# conventions. Licences and attribution are in references/CREDITS.md — read it
# before reusing these, one set is CC-BY-SA (ShareAlike), the rest are CC0.
!references/**/*.png

# projectmem. events.jsonl is the append-only source of truth that summary.md
# is regenerated from, so it IS committed — ignoring it would mean the memory
# does not survive a clone. Only the runtime/derived files are ignored:
# watch.pid/watch.log belong to the local `pjm watch` daemon, and
# structure.json is a rebuildable code-structure cache, and .current_issue is
# a transient pointer to whichever issue this machine is working on.
#
# The spool is where the AUTOMATIC writers (the post-commit/post-merge
# auto-capture hooks and the churn daemon) stage events, so they never write to
# a tracked file outside a commit and leave the tree dirty behind it. The
# pre-commit hook folds it into events.jsonl and stages both.
.projectmem/.current_issue
.projectmem/watch.pid
.projectmem/watch.log
.projectmem/structure.json
.projectmem/events.spool.jsonl
.projectmem/events.spool.consuming.jsonl
